  "apocryphaNote": "If you open a Catholic Bible (RSVCE / NRSVCE) to Daniel 3, you will find a long prayer and a song between what Protestants number as 3:23 and 3:24 — the Prayer of Azariah and the Song of the Three Jews. It is in the Greek Daniel (Septuagint / Theodotion), not in the Hebrew-Aramaic text that the Protestant Old Testament follows. Jerome knew the difference and put these additions in a second rank. Reformers followed the Hebrew canon. That is the short 'why it was left out' — not a conspiracy, a decision about which manuscript family counts as Daniel. The prayer is worth reading as what faithful Jews imagined those three men saying in the fire. Switch to NRSVCE in the toolbar if you want to see the extra verses on the screen. We are not asking this Baptist room to call it Scripture equal to Isaiah. We are asking why a whole prayer disappeared from one family of Bibles and survived in another."
